interface InvalidRequestError {
   message: string;
   data?: unknown;
   code: -32600;
}A JSON-RPC error indicating that the request is not a valid request object. This error is returned when the message structure does not conform to the JSON-RPC 2.0 specification requirements for a request (e.g., missing required fields like `jsonrpc` or `method`, or using invalid types for these fields). See JSON-RPC 2.0 Error Object message: string A short description of the error. The message SHOULD be limited to a concise single sentence. Inherited from Error. message data?: unknown Additional information about the error. The value of this member is defined by the sender (e.g. detailed error information, nested errors etc.). Inherited from Error. data code: -32600 The error type that occurred. Overrides Error. code
